# deepseek-coder-v2:instruct — the chat/instruct sibling of deepseek-coder-v2:fim
# on timmy's RX 9070 XT, with a baked context so it can load at all.
#
# Why this tag exists: the library tag deepseek-coder-v2:16b-lite-instruct-q4_0
# has no num_ctx, so it inherits OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH=131072. With
# OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL=2 ollama launched `llama-server -c 262144 -np 2`, a 36.7 GiB
# q8_0 KV cache. llama.cpp's fit step put only 10 of 28 layers on the GPU and
# spilled ~31 GiB to host RAM, and the kernel OOM-killed the daemon at the
# ollama.service MemoryMax=16G (2026-09-16, twice; TASK-1216 / IDEA-1105).
#
# num_ctx 8192 matches deepseek-coder-v2:fim and pairs with OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL=4:
# 4 x 8192 slots = 4.5 GiB q8_0 KV + 8.2 GiB weights, which fits the 16 GiB card
# alone. Budget is 3 summarize requests + 1 FIM; keep VLM prompts under ~7k
# tokens. OLLAMA_MAX_LOADED_MODELS=1, so loading this tag evicts the FIM runner.
#
# Template and stops (User:/Assistant:) are inherited from the library tag.
# Requires: ollama pull deepseek-coder-v2:16b-lite-instruct-q4_0
# Build:    ollama create deepseek-coder-v2:instruct -f deepseek-coder-v2-instruct.Modelfile

FROM deepseek-coder-v2:16b-lite-instruct-q4_0

# num_ctx baked so the runner never inherits the 131072 server default (see above).
PARAMETER num_ctx 8192
